// why: the base tsconfig.json excludes "src/**/*.test.ts", and the package's
// only scripts are `build` (tsc, which honours that exclusion) and `test`
// (tsx, which transpiles without typechecking). The consequence is that engine
// test files have NEVER been compiled, so every `satisfies`-based drift pin in
// the suite is documentation rather than a gate — including pins whose own
// comments promise compile-time enforcement (WP-557 / WP-563, D-24372).
//
// why: this config sets "noEmit" precisely so the shipped build is unaffected.
// It typechecks the test files and writes nothing; `pnpm -r build` output stays
// byte-identical because only tsconfig.json feeds the `build` script.
//
// why: NOT wired into CI yet (D-24372 §2). A required check carrying hundreds
// of known pre-existing errors would block every unrelated PR. Wiring lands
// with the final cleanup packet, when the count reaches zero.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
